<urn:atm:triage:finding/AW-READY-O5>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AW-READY-O5" ;
  triage:title "RULE-001/ADR-020 still name the legacy-daemon module as the sole sc-observability import exception owner; the new RetainedLogger facade also leaks backend types through its public signatures, violating ADR-020's opacity condition" ;
  triage:description "fenix-C architecture/boundaries review (01M1S751VVM0K4C7ZW6YDPC7BQ, their F5). RULE-001 (.claude/agents/arch-qa.md:59-65) and ADR-020's review conditions still confine the sc-observability import exception to a specific legacy-daemon module; AW1-QA-B2 (an already-closed finding in this phase's original 70-record ledger) was closed by MOVING the import to atm-observability rather than updating the rule/ADR text to name the new owner -- a textually-unreconciled second exception. Additionally the new facade (RetainedLogger) leaks backend types (sc_observability_types::LoggingHealthReport/LogEvent/ServiceName/Level) through its own public signatures, violating ADR-020's own opacity condition. quality-mgr accepts this on specific file/line/paragraph citation; this is the clearest instance this phase of the pre-existing Family D pattern (a rule enforced at one point silently grows a second, textually-unreconciled exception). Fix: update RULE-001/ADR-020 text to name atm-observability as the current owner; wrap/re-export opaque facade types instead of leaking sc_observability_types directly through RetainedLogger's public API." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-aw" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "boundary-contract" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-05T18:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
